1
00:00:16,789 --> 00:00:18,082
[alarm beeps]

2
00:00:19,959 --> 00:00:22,169
[theme music playing]

3
00:00:58,664 --> 00:00:59,498
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

4
00:00:59,582 --> 00:01:01,083
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED FOR SOME SCENES

5
00:01:04,044 --> 00:01:07,339
Well, I think I'm going to resign
from SAEUM.

6
00:01:08,257 --> 00:01:09,300
What?

7
00:01:10,009 --> 00:01:11,093
I'm going to resign.

8
00:01:11,886 --> 00:01:13,679
Why would you think about resigning?

9
00:01:13,762 --> 00:01:14,763
It's cold.

10
00:01:14,847 --> 00:01:16,015
Let's go talk inside.

11
00:01:17,099 --> 00:01:20,436
[gentle music playing]

12
00:01:31,405 --> 00:01:33,115
Warm up your hands first.

13
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:35,784
I guess my hunch was right.

14
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:38,913
You suddenly taking a day off,

15
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,041
and saying all of those weird things.

16
00:01:42,708 --> 00:01:44,543
I always seem to get caught by you.

17
00:01:44,627 --> 00:01:46,170
Yeah, but still,

18
00:01:46,253 --> 00:01:48,547
I didn't think
you'd actually consider resigning.

19
00:01:48,631 --> 00:01:52,676
You were going to be the first person
I told once I'd sorted out my thoughts.

20
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,887
If working together is the issue,

21
00:01:54,970 --> 00:01:57,097
I can just transfer
to the Development Team.

22
00:01:57,181 --> 00:02:00,059
You should stay where you are
doing the work you want to do.

23
00:02:00,142 --> 00:02:01,393
But what about you?

24
00:02:01,477 --> 00:02:02,478
I…

25
00:02:04,396 --> 00:02:06,273
I don't have that anymore.

26
00:02:06,357 --> 00:02:07,399
Why not?

27
00:02:07,483 --> 00:02:11,236
I've come this far determined to prove
myself through my work, not politics.

28
00:02:11,737 --> 00:02:14,657
But at this rate,
even if I get to the next level,

29
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:17,159
I'll still end up doing things
I don't want to do.

30
00:02:17,242 --> 00:02:19,161
And that's not what I really want.

31
00:02:19,244 --> 00:02:23,040
You know, even at another company,
it won't be any different.

32
00:02:23,123 --> 00:02:24,375
I know.

33
00:02:24,458 --> 00:02:26,752
That's why I'm not saying
I'll just move to another job.

34
00:02:26,835 --> 00:02:28,796
I would like to hit pause for a moment.

35
00:02:28,879 --> 00:02:31,006
I want to remember
why I started this work,

36
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:32,675
where my destination is,

37
00:02:32,758 --> 00:02:35,594
and what I would truly want to do
from now on.

38
00:02:36,095 --> 00:02:37,262
[sighs]

39
00:02:37,888 --> 00:02:39,056
I don't know.

40
00:02:40,724 --> 00:02:42,518
As your girlfriend,

41
00:02:42,601 --> 00:02:45,020
I want to support the decision
that you're making.

42
00:02:45,771 --> 00:02:48,816
But as your colleague,
I want to talk you out of it.

43
00:02:49,525 --> 00:02:51,193
But it feels like a waste

44
00:02:52,027 --> 00:02:54,655
to throw away everything you've built
over the years,

45
00:02:55,364 --> 00:02:57,032
and everything that would've followed.

46
00:02:57,116 --> 00:02:58,826
None of that matters to me.

47
00:02:58,909 --> 00:03:01,078
I just want to be with you
without all this stress,

48
00:03:01,161 --> 00:03:02,955
doing the work I actually want to do.

49
00:03:04,289 --> 00:03:05,290
[sighs]

50
00:03:17,886 --> 00:03:18,887
Thank you, sir.

51
00:03:18,971 --> 00:03:20,806
No, I should be thanking you.

52
00:03:20,889 --> 00:03:24,184
Buying all this beef
for this old geezer's birthday.

53
00:03:24,268 --> 00:03:25,644
[both chuckle]

54
00:03:25,728 --> 00:03:27,521
I wish you a happy birthday, sir.

55
00:03:27,604 --> 00:03:28,731
[chuckles]

56
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:33,819
You must've been surprised
to hear he's suddenly leaving the company.

57
00:03:34,403 --> 00:03:36,655
[chuckles] Yes.

58
00:03:37,156 --> 00:03:41,160
To be honest,
I'm still feeling quite overwhelmed, sir.

59
00:03:42,411 --> 00:03:44,830
You know, when Si-woo makes a decision,

60
00:03:45,748 --> 00:03:48,500
it's only after he's tried
absolutely everything he could.

61
00:03:51,128 --> 00:03:53,088
Yes, I know that.

62
00:03:54,256 --> 00:03:56,842
But that's what's so upsetting.

63
00:03:58,302 --> 00:03:59,803
Why does he always

64
00:03:59,887 --> 00:04:03,265
try to go through hard times
all by himself like that?

65
00:04:05,476 --> 00:04:07,352
I can see why Si-woo fell for you.

66
00:04:07,436 --> 00:04:08,479
[chuckles]

67
00:04:08,979 --> 00:04:10,272
[chuckles]

68
00:04:10,355 --> 00:04:12,274
Have you two enjoyed
talking behind my back?

69
00:04:12,858 --> 00:04:14,860
-[parent chuckles]
-Yes.

70
00:04:14,943 --> 00:04:18,655
I said I was really worried you wouldn't
be as charming outside the office.

71
00:04:19,865 --> 00:04:20,949
That sounds like a threat.

72
00:04:23,327 --> 00:04:24,495
Must be nice

73
00:04:24,578 --> 00:04:27,247
having someone
to pull you back. [exclaims]

74
00:04:28,123 --> 00:04:30,084
Yes, it's nice.

75
00:04:30,834 --> 00:04:32,836
[gentle music playing]

76
00:04:37,174 --> 00:04:38,175
[chuckles]

77
00:04:39,093 --> 00:04:40,594
Why do you look so lost in thought?

78
00:04:41,095 --> 00:04:46,475
Well, I'm just wondering how involved
I'm allowed to be in your life, you know?

79
00:04:46,558 --> 00:04:48,310
You can be involved in all of it.

80
00:04:50,646 --> 00:04:51,522
Okay.

81
00:04:52,314 --> 00:04:53,982
When are you going to resign?

82
00:04:54,066 --> 00:04:55,567
What company will you work for?

83
00:04:55,651 --> 00:04:57,861
Or are you starting a business?

84
00:04:57,945 --> 00:04:59,363
You're not going overseas, are you?

85
00:04:59,446 --> 00:05:01,365
Should I put together a slide deck
and report to you?

86
00:05:01,448 --> 00:05:03,367
Hey, I'm being serious right now.

87
00:05:03,450 --> 00:05:04,993
I'll submit my resignation soon,

88
00:05:05,077 --> 00:05:07,371
and then I'll take my time
figuring out the rest.

89
00:05:07,454 --> 00:05:08,539
[sighs]

90
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:11,416
So you really don't have a plan at all.

91
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,001
[chuckles]

92
00:05:16,755 --> 00:05:18,090
Is this not the right way?

93
00:05:19,091 --> 00:05:21,260
Ji-yoon, could you check the GPS for me?

94
00:05:21,343 --> 00:05:22,845
Uh, sure.

95
00:05:23,637 --> 00:05:25,889
I think you took a wrong turn
at that fork earlier.

96
00:05:25,973 --> 00:05:27,891
We're going to have to take
quite the detour.

97
00:05:27,975 --> 00:05:30,769
Ah. I couldn't tell in the dark.

98
00:05:30,853 --> 00:05:33,188
I guess you don't know
everything after all.

99
00:05:33,772 --> 00:05:34,773
I knew it.

100
00:05:34,857 --> 00:05:36,775
I'll just have to coach you
from the passenger seat.

101
00:05:37,943 --> 00:05:39,486
Well, I'm in your hands now.

102
00:05:40,737 --> 00:05:42,948
I can't say I'm completely on board yet,

103
00:05:43,574 --> 00:05:45,617
but I want us to figure it out together.

104
00:05:45,701 --> 00:05:46,702
[chuckles]

105
00:05:48,036 --> 00:05:49,580
[sighs]

106
00:05:50,581 --> 00:05:51,665
Thank you for everything.

107
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:57,504
[sighs] You know, I wonder if the company
will let you walk away that easily.

108
00:05:59,464 --> 00:06:00,632
[sighs]

109
00:06:04,761 --> 00:06:07,723
EPISODE 12

110
00:06:07,806 --> 00:06:11,935
NO MAP TO FOLLOW,
STILL CLOCKING IN!

111
00:06:14,521 --> 00:06:16,064
What did you just say now?

112
00:06:16,148 --> 00:06:17,274
I'm handing in my notice.

113
00:06:17,357 --> 00:06:18,275
Si-woo.

114
00:06:18,358 --> 00:06:20,277
I wanted to tell you directly

115
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,196
before officially submitting
my resignation.

116
00:06:22,279 --> 00:06:23,280
Wait,

117
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:26,033
is this because
Ms. Cha's promotion fell through?

118
00:06:26,116 --> 00:06:28,493
I am displeased
with our evaluation system,

119
00:06:28,577 --> 00:06:32,289
and disappointed by our conservative
attitude toward new ideas.

120
00:06:32,372 --> 00:06:33,624
But despite all of that,

121
00:06:33,707 --> 00:06:36,501
I've come to the conclusion that
I'm simply not fit for this organization.

122
00:06:36,585 --> 00:06:37,586
Thus my decision.

123
00:06:37,669 --> 00:06:40,255
That's why we should change
the organization together.

124
00:06:40,339 --> 00:06:42,174
You can't just change it, President Han.

125
00:06:44,259 --> 00:06:45,886
Your position won't allow it.

126
00:06:46,595 --> 00:06:48,263
And neither will mine, ma'am.

127
00:06:49,973 --> 00:06:51,391
Think it over again.

128
00:06:52,351 --> 00:06:55,771
Losing you would be a massive loss
for me and the company.

129
00:06:55,854 --> 00:06:56,980
[inhales deeply]

130
00:06:57,606 --> 00:06:58,774
I will tender my resignation.

131
00:06:58,857 --> 00:07:00,192
You can't!

132
00:07:02,319 --> 00:07:03,320
Just wait.

133
00:07:09,034 --> 00:07:10,035
[sighs]

134
00:07:12,621 --> 00:07:16,083
Everything discussed in this room today
is strictly confidential.

135
00:07:16,166 --> 00:07:17,167
Yes, ma'am.

136
00:07:17,751 --> 00:07:18,752
Yes.

137
00:07:19,670 --> 00:07:21,672
Manager Kang Si-woo wishes to resign.

138
00:07:23,507 --> 00:07:25,550
-[HR lead] But Mr. Kang is…
-[U-jin] Yes.

139
00:07:26,134 --> 00:07:28,470
He's a key asset
specially managed by the company.

140
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:31,723
Apologies, ma'am.

141
00:07:31,807 --> 00:07:33,934
We missed his flight risk signals.

142
00:07:35,018 --> 00:07:37,229
You seem quite surprised, Mr. Noh,

143
00:07:37,312 --> 00:07:39,606
to learn that the man
you've been desperate to drag down

144
00:07:39,690 --> 00:07:41,316
is actually a key asset.

145
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:43,026
It must be a lot to process.

146
00:07:43,568 --> 00:07:46,196
I will try to convince him
with a better compensation package

147
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,281
or a new role.

148
00:07:47,364 --> 00:07:48,699
That won't work with him.

149
00:07:51,034 --> 00:07:54,162
Just make sure
to keep an eye out for his resignation,

150
00:07:54,246 --> 00:07:56,707
and once it comes through,
hold the approval.

151
00:07:56,790 --> 00:08:00,544
In the meantime,
I'd like you, Mr. Noh, to speak to him.

152
00:08:00,627 --> 00:08:01,503
Me?

153
00:08:01,586 --> 00:08:04,256
You are his supervising executive
after all.

154
00:08:04,339 --> 00:08:05,173
Yeah.

155
00:08:05,257 --> 00:08:08,176
If you go down as the executive
who let a key asset slip away,

156
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,971
I doubt you'll score well
on your next performance review.

157
00:08:11,596 --> 00:08:13,098
-[sighs]
-[U-jin] Keep Kang Si-woo

158
00:08:13,181 --> 00:08:15,100
in the company at all costs.

159
00:08:15,892 --> 00:08:18,645
Because I will hold you
personally accountable for the outcome.

160
00:08:19,730 --> 00:08:20,772
Answer me.

161
00:08:23,442 --> 00:08:24,484
Yes, ma'am.

162
00:08:31,366 --> 00:08:33,076
So what are you planning to do now?

163
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:35,370
We improve his work environment first.

164
00:08:36,413 --> 00:08:39,833
Forget waiting
for Ko's disciplinary decision.

165
00:08:39,916 --> 00:08:41,084
Have him removed immediately.

166
00:08:41,168 --> 00:08:42,169
Yes.

167
00:08:44,379 --> 00:08:45,380
[sighs]

168
00:08:52,804 --> 00:08:53,930
[sighs]

169
00:09:05,734 --> 00:09:07,444
[breathing heavily]

170
00:09:09,738 --> 00:09:13,200
I bet you're thrilled now that
you won't be running into me for a while.

171
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:16,953
"For a while."

172
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,750
-It'll be longer than that.
-What?

173
00:09:22,334 --> 00:09:24,044
You really think I'll be gone for good?

174
00:09:24,127 --> 00:09:25,420
Just wait.

175
00:09:25,504 --> 00:09:28,840
When I get back, you're the first one
I'm pushing out of this company. Geez.

176
00:09:29,758 --> 00:09:31,468
All right. I look forward to it.

177
00:09:31,551 --> 00:09:34,179
[scoffing, clicks tongue]

178
00:09:34,262 --> 00:09:37,474
Y-You've been an insufferable prick
from day one, you know that?

179
00:09:37,557 --> 00:09:40,310
My entire life went downhill
the moment I met you.

180
00:09:40,394 --> 00:09:42,312
[breathing heavily]

181
00:09:43,647 --> 00:09:47,025
And you know I would've been different
if I hadn't had you as a boss.

182
00:09:47,109 --> 00:09:47,984
What?

183
00:09:48,068 --> 00:09:51,321
It seems like you don't have much luck
with bosses either.

184
00:09:55,492 --> 00:09:57,619
[scoffing]

185
00:10:00,664 --> 00:10:01,873
You take this one.

186
00:10:01,957 --> 00:10:03,875
I'll wait and catch the next one.

187
00:10:03,959 --> 00:10:06,920
-[huffs] Hey, no, are you really…
-[electronic voice] Doors closing.

188
00:10:07,796 --> 00:10:09,172
An accountant?

189
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,383
What does he look like?

190
00:10:12,134 --> 00:10:13,552
It's just… [chuckles]

191
00:10:13,635 --> 00:10:16,847
Ji-yoon cares more
about a guy's looks than his job.

192
00:10:17,431 --> 00:10:18,765
Oh, really?

193
00:10:20,016 --> 00:10:23,061
In that case,
I'll go ahead and ask her about it.

194
00:10:23,562 --> 00:10:24,813
All right.

195
00:10:31,361 --> 00:10:33,113
[lighthearted music playing]

196
00:10:33,196 --> 00:10:34,781
Why are you suddenly acting so strange?

197
00:10:34,865 --> 00:10:37,075
Isn't this the kind of thing you wanted?

198
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,914
So sour.

199
00:10:43,498 --> 00:10:45,083
Just leave Ji-yoon alone.

200
00:10:45,584 --> 00:10:48,170
I don't like hearing her nagging either.

201
00:10:49,296 --> 00:10:53,467
But people won't stop pestering me
because she works at SAEUM.

202
00:10:54,092 --> 00:10:55,343
What about that regular?

203
00:10:55,427 --> 00:10:57,304
I told you to set them up.
What's the holdup?

204
00:10:57,387 --> 00:10:59,097
[groans] Set them up? Come on.

205
00:10:59,181 --> 00:11:00,640
They'll meet if it's meant to be.

206
00:11:00,724 --> 00:11:03,852
The company is too big
for them to meet by chance.

207
00:11:04,936 --> 00:11:06,521
What, is he not that great of a guy?

208
00:11:06,605 --> 00:11:08,940
Oh, why are you putting words in my mouth?

209
00:11:09,024 --> 00:11:11,735
Do you really think I'd have a drink
with someone who wasn't that great?

210
00:11:11,818 --> 00:11:13,528
That's exactly my point.

211
00:11:13,612 --> 00:11:15,739
Who would want to hang out
with a boring guy like you, huh?

212
00:11:15,822 --> 00:11:17,949
-Hey.
-What's his position?

213
00:11:18,033 --> 00:11:20,410
Does he live alone? Are his parents alive?

214
00:11:21,870 --> 00:11:24,122
Look at you,
giving me that silent treatment.

215
00:11:24,206 --> 00:11:26,791
If you don't want to get involved,
just give me his number.

216
00:11:26,875 --> 00:11:28,793
Mmm. [grunts]

217
00:11:37,302 --> 00:11:38,470
Hey, that's my phone.

218
00:11:38,553 --> 00:11:40,305
What's yours is still mine.

219
00:11:41,223 --> 00:11:42,224
[groans]

220
00:11:43,058 --> 00:11:44,059
Where are you going?

221
00:11:44,684 --> 00:11:46,311
Hey, we need to go see that lawyer.

222
00:11:46,394 --> 00:11:47,437
I won't.

223
00:11:49,773 --> 00:11:50,774
[chuckles]

224
00:11:50,857 --> 00:11:53,568
Great job, everyone,
on the Home-AI launch.

225
00:11:55,111 --> 00:11:58,823
The Sales and Marketing Team will take
over the remaining workload from here.

226
00:11:58,907 --> 00:12:00,825
So what are we going to work on next?

227
00:12:00,909 --> 00:12:02,410
As of today, this team…

228
00:12:02,494 --> 00:12:04,579
[imitates drumroll]

229
00:12:05,163 --> 00:12:06,206
…will be disbanding.

230
00:12:08,166 --> 00:12:09,918
-What?
-All of a sudden?

231
00:12:10,001 --> 00:12:11,044
[sighs]

232
00:12:11,127 --> 00:12:13,296
I'll do my best
to ensure everyone transfers

233
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:15,257
to the department of their choice.

234
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:16,383
Mr. Kang.

235
00:12:19,052 --> 00:12:21,805
In that case, I'd like to head back
to Product Planning Team 1.

236
00:12:21,888 --> 00:12:22,889
Sure.

237
00:12:23,515 --> 00:12:25,892
Let me know
once you two make up your minds.

238
00:12:25,976 --> 00:12:28,895
But I was thinking of our next project.

239
00:12:29,479 --> 00:12:31,189
You can do that
with your respective teams.

240
00:12:31,273 --> 00:12:32,774
What can I do there?

241
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:36,611
They'll just tell me
to stick to the established ways.

242
00:12:37,112 --> 00:12:39,906
I can't work the way I do now
under any other boss.

243
00:12:40,657 --> 00:12:44,160
Look, what if we came up
with a new project idea?

244
00:12:44,244 --> 00:12:45,787
We'll pull all-nighters if we have to

245
00:12:45,870 --> 00:12:48,123
and find something
the higher-ups can't resist.

246
00:12:49,624 --> 00:12:53,086
Can't you just stay on
as our boss, Mr. Kang?

247
00:12:54,588 --> 00:12:56,089
[sighs]

248
00:12:57,882 --> 00:13:01,469
You three are the driving force
behind Home-AI's success.

249
00:13:02,429 --> 00:13:04,889
No matter your boss or the team you're on,

250
00:13:04,973 --> 00:13:06,933
work with your heads held high.

251
00:13:07,017 --> 00:13:08,810
You have completely earned that right.

252
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:11,688
-[sighs]
-[phone buzzes]

253
00:13:18,612 --> 00:13:21,239
Here. Use this.
Grab a nice lunch together.

254
00:13:22,824 --> 00:13:23,992
What about you, sir?

255
00:13:24,075 --> 00:13:25,368
Something urgent came up.

256
00:13:25,452 --> 00:13:26,578
I'll join next time.

257
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:31,708
[sighs]

258
00:13:31,791 --> 00:13:33,251
What's going on here?

259
00:13:33,335 --> 00:13:35,962
The task force was always temporary.

260
00:13:36,046 --> 00:13:39,215
It's normal we're getting dissolved
now that the project is over.

261
00:13:39,299 --> 00:13:41,468
And Mr. Kang? What is he going to do now?

262
00:13:41,551 --> 00:13:43,887
Oh, is he taking Mr. Ko's position?

263
00:13:43,970 --> 00:13:45,889
And that's why
you're transferring there, right?

264
00:13:45,972 --> 00:13:48,725
Oh, no. Mr. Kang
won't be going anywhere for a while.

265
00:13:49,309 --> 00:13:50,602
What's that supposed to mean?

266
00:13:50,685 --> 00:13:52,729
-He says nothing is decided yet.
-[phone buzzes]

267
00:13:54,981 --> 00:13:58,026
Oh. You guys go get some lunch.

268
00:14:00,654 --> 00:14:01,946
Hey, Ji-yoon…

269
00:14:05,617 --> 00:14:06,618
[sighs]

270
00:14:07,118 --> 00:14:08,119
[sighs]

271
00:14:09,871 --> 00:14:10,872
[sighs]

272
00:14:10,955 --> 00:14:12,374
Mom,

273
00:14:12,457 --> 00:14:14,584
this is so rude to the other person.

274
00:14:14,668 --> 00:14:16,544
I told you I don't want to…

275
00:14:16,628 --> 00:14:17,629
So…

276
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:25,637
Is he my blind date, Mother?

277
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:27,764
[Hye-gyeong] He seems like a great guy.

278
00:14:27,847 --> 00:14:28,932
He works at SAEUM too,

279
00:14:29,015 --> 00:14:31,101
so you can see each other
even when you're busy.

280
00:14:31,184 --> 00:14:32,727
Mom, let me call you back.

281
00:14:38,191 --> 00:14:40,235
Was this your urgent matter?

282
00:14:42,862 --> 00:14:44,447
Did your mother ask you to come here too?

283
00:14:44,531 --> 00:14:48,493
Oh… I see. You came here
to meet with my mom, right?

284
00:14:48,576 --> 00:14:50,495
And yet you didn't say
a single word to me?

285
00:14:50,578 --> 00:14:52,414
I wasn't sure
what she wanted to talk about.

286
00:14:52,497 --> 00:14:54,958
Still, you should've given me a heads-up.

287
00:14:55,041 --> 00:14:56,835
I had no idea what was going…

288
00:14:56,918 --> 00:14:58,420
[gasps, sighs]

289
00:15:02,799 --> 00:15:04,759
Wait, was this lunch
meant to be a blind date?

290
00:15:06,261 --> 00:15:07,262
[chuckles]

291
00:15:09,055 --> 00:15:12,517
Oh… So you came to a blind date
behind my back?

292
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:16,938
I didn't. I only came
to politely turn the guy down.

293
00:15:17,897 --> 00:15:19,065
[scoffs]

294
00:15:19,149 --> 00:15:20,567
[chuckles]

295
00:15:22,026 --> 00:15:25,488
You know, my mom must've
really taken a liking to you.

296
00:15:25,572 --> 00:15:27,365
Wow, what a relief. [sighs]

297
00:15:28,199 --> 00:15:29,200
But what do we do now?

298
00:15:29,784 --> 00:15:33,246
Guess we should tell her the truth
before she catches us.

299
00:15:34,664 --> 00:15:35,832
Yeah.

300
00:15:36,416 --> 00:15:38,918
[breathes deeply]

301
00:15:43,089 --> 00:15:44,632
Oh, hello.

302
00:15:45,717 --> 00:15:46,843
How can I help you?

303
00:15:47,552 --> 00:15:51,848
Uh, so is Jae-in in here by any chance?

304
00:15:51,931 --> 00:15:53,475
Oh, he just stepped out.

305
00:15:53,558 --> 00:15:54,559
Oh. [sighs]

306
00:15:55,351 --> 00:15:57,562
You're No-ah, right?

307
00:15:57,645 --> 00:15:58,980
Wait, you know who I am?

308
00:15:59,063 --> 00:16:02,650
Of course. Jae-in doesn't stop bragging
about his girlfriend. [chuckles]

309
00:16:04,861 --> 00:16:05,862
He'll be back soon.

310
00:16:09,115 --> 00:16:10,325
Seung-jun, I forgot my…

311
00:16:19,459 --> 00:16:20,460
Why are you here?

312
00:16:22,712 --> 00:16:24,214
Because I don't want to lose you.

313
00:16:25,882 --> 00:16:28,009
I know how selfish I'm being right now.

314
00:16:28,968 --> 00:16:32,514
I don't want to break up with you,
and I still want to go to Senegal.

315
00:16:34,474 --> 00:16:37,936
But I really don't want
to give up on either one.

316
00:16:41,022 --> 00:16:42,023
[sighs]

317
00:16:47,278 --> 00:16:49,864
I grew up moving constantly
because of my dad's job.

318
00:16:51,241 --> 00:16:54,953
People envied me,
but I never had real friends.

319
00:16:55,036 --> 00:16:56,955
Every time I made one, we moved.

320
00:16:58,081 --> 00:17:02,001
I came to Korea because
I wanted to live here when I turned 20,

321
00:17:02,544 --> 00:17:04,379
even if it meant being all alone.

322
00:17:06,047 --> 00:17:08,716
Now, I finally have people
I can call friends,

323
00:17:09,676 --> 00:17:11,469
and there's so much I want to do here.

324
00:17:13,346 --> 00:17:14,806
So right now…

325
00:17:17,642 --> 00:17:19,602
I'm unable to follow you.

326
00:17:21,896 --> 00:17:24,023
And I can't handle long distance either.

327
00:17:24,649 --> 00:17:27,110
[sighs] I don't know if I can either.

328
00:17:27,610 --> 00:17:29,112
The thing is…

329
00:17:30,363 --> 00:17:32,866
I can't bear the thought
of ever losing you.

330
00:17:41,207 --> 00:17:42,125
Sorry.

331
00:17:43,084 --> 00:17:44,586
[inhales shakily]

332
00:17:44,669 --> 00:17:46,087
I don't think I can do this.

333
00:17:50,341 --> 00:17:52,969
[exhales shakily] Actually…

334
00:17:54,429 --> 00:17:56,097
I'm the one who's sorry.

335
00:18:07,317 --> 00:18:08,318
[sighs]

336
00:18:13,531 --> 00:18:16,534
[scoffs] What happened to being miserable
when you don't see her?

337
00:18:16,618 --> 00:18:18,244
I feel that way.

338
00:18:18,328 --> 00:18:19,787
That's why I'm doing this.

339
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,540
I don't know the details,

340
00:18:22,624 --> 00:18:25,460
but look, the dumbest thing you can do

341
00:18:25,543 --> 00:18:28,087
is force an end to something
that isn't over yet.

342
00:18:30,131 --> 00:18:31,382
I know how it'll end.

343
00:18:31,466 --> 00:18:33,176
Hey, you're getting cocky, kid.

344
00:18:33,676 --> 00:18:36,346
How would you know
if you haven't even gone there yet, huh?

345
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:38,389
[sighs]

346
00:18:45,605 --> 00:18:48,107
[chuckles] Do you like it?

347
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:52,111
Mmm, yes, I do, of course,
but gosh. [inhales sharply]

348
00:18:52,195 --> 00:18:54,948
I don't know how many times a year
I'd wear a coat this expensive.

349
00:18:55,031 --> 00:18:56,449
Just wear it all the time.

350
00:18:56,532 --> 00:18:58,034
Wear it when you see your friends,

351
00:18:58,117 --> 00:19:00,662
or when you go out on dates with Dad.

352
00:19:00,745 --> 00:19:02,538
Why would I go on dates with your dad?

353
00:19:02,622 --> 00:19:04,415
I see him at home all day. [scoffs]

354
00:19:04,999 --> 00:19:08,127
It seems like
he's trying really hard, though.

355
00:19:08,753 --> 00:19:11,047
Are you still set
on graduating from marriage?

356
00:19:11,130 --> 00:19:14,342
Years of resentment
aren't erased that easily. [scoffs]

357
00:19:14,425 --> 00:19:15,927
Let's see if he keeps this up.

358
00:19:16,010 --> 00:19:17,387
I get it.

359
00:19:18,221 --> 00:19:20,723
But it sounds like there's still
a glimmer of hope, right?

360
00:19:22,350 --> 00:19:23,935
Why aren't you saying anything?

361
00:19:24,018 --> 00:19:27,981
I thought you'd throw a fit,
but you got me clothes and a meal.

362
00:19:29,148 --> 00:19:30,942
Do you actually like the guy?

363
00:19:32,944 --> 00:19:35,071
Mmm. [chuckles]

364
00:19:35,738 --> 00:19:37,073
I like him very much.

365
00:19:37,156 --> 00:19:39,033
Really? I knew it!

366
00:19:39,117 --> 00:19:41,160
Because he totally won me over too!

367
00:19:41,661 --> 00:19:43,746
So, did you start dating?

368
00:19:45,248 --> 00:19:46,457
Actually,

369
00:19:47,166 --> 00:19:49,502
we were already seeing each other.

370
00:19:50,670 --> 00:19:53,715
Manager Kang Si-woo
is my team lead at work.

371
00:19:54,549 --> 00:19:55,591
Hmm?

372
00:19:55,675 --> 00:19:58,594
At first, I liked him as a coworker,

373
00:19:59,929 --> 00:20:02,140
then I liked him as a man, and…

374
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:05,601
and now… now I'm in love with him.

375
00:20:06,102 --> 00:20:08,271
You mean you're already a couple?

376
00:20:09,147 --> 00:20:09,981
Mmm.

377
00:20:10,064 --> 00:20:11,315
I can't believe it!

378
00:20:11,858 --> 00:20:13,651
Oh, I had no idea.

379
00:20:13,735 --> 00:20:16,404
And here I was, trying to play matchmaker.

380
00:20:16,487 --> 00:20:19,282
Wait, hold on,
so did your father not know either?

381
00:20:19,365 --> 00:20:22,577
He actually caught us together
a little while ago,

382
00:20:23,494 --> 00:20:26,497
but he probably
couldn't bring himself to tell you.

383
00:20:26,581 --> 00:20:27,665
Why not?

384
00:20:27,749 --> 00:20:30,585
Why couldn't he tell me
about two of his favorite people dating?

385
00:20:31,377 --> 00:20:32,545
Because…

386
00:20:35,131 --> 00:20:36,924
he's been through a divorce.

387
00:20:39,469 --> 00:20:40,470
What?

388
00:20:59,697 --> 00:21:01,741
You would've had to cross
that bridge eventually.

389
00:21:02,909 --> 00:21:04,285
Just trust Ji-yoon and wait.

390
00:21:05,078 --> 00:21:06,579
Are you rooting for me?

391
00:21:06,662 --> 00:21:08,289
Why would I be rooting for you?

392
00:21:09,707 --> 00:21:11,000
I'm rooting for my daughter.

393
00:21:11,584 --> 00:21:13,044
[chuckles]

394
00:21:13,127 --> 00:21:14,962
I'll say it again and again,

395
00:21:15,505 --> 00:21:17,715
I'm on my wife's side, no matter what.

396
00:21:18,424 --> 00:21:19,550
That's just how it is.

397
00:21:19,634 --> 00:21:21,719
It's all right. Someone's on my side too.

398
00:21:21,803 --> 00:21:22,929
That's my daughter!

399
00:21:23,012 --> 00:21:24,514
[chuckles]

400
00:21:26,682 --> 00:21:29,477
If she disapproves, what will you do?

401
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,062
I'll have to wait

402
00:21:31,562 --> 00:21:33,397
until Mother finally warms up to me.

403
00:21:35,358 --> 00:21:37,360
[smacks lips] Wait, hold on.

404
00:21:38,194 --> 00:21:40,822
How come you call her "Mother"
and I'm just "Mister"?

405
00:21:40,905 --> 00:21:43,991
[chuckles] All right,
then please help me out,

406
00:21:44,075 --> 00:21:45,451
Father.

407
00:21:48,371 --> 00:21:50,414
As if I stand a chance against my wife.

408
00:21:54,794 --> 00:21:57,755
You can't just storm out like that
without hearing me out first!

409
00:21:57,839 --> 00:21:59,924
I already said no.
What more is there to hear?

410
00:22:00,007 --> 00:22:01,008
Why not?

411
00:22:01,092 --> 00:22:03,261
You were thinking
about ending your marriage too, Mom.

412
00:22:03,344 --> 00:22:04,971
You of all people should understand him.

413
00:22:05,054 --> 00:22:06,889
Yes, I'm dying to end my marriage!

414
00:22:08,141 --> 00:22:10,726
Because I've been holding it in
all these years.

415
00:22:11,853 --> 00:22:15,022
All married couples have felt
like splitting up at one point.

416
00:22:15,606 --> 00:22:17,984
But they stick it out
and try to make it work.

417
00:22:19,026 --> 00:22:20,278
But he…

418
00:22:20,361 --> 00:22:22,363
he got a divorce in less than a year?

419
00:22:23,698 --> 00:22:25,825
How can you trust someone
who gives up that easily?

420
00:22:25,908 --> 00:22:29,704
Sticking it out and making it work
is something you do together.

421
00:22:29,787 --> 00:22:32,915
But Mr. Kang…
He never even got the chance to do that.

422
00:22:32,999 --> 00:22:35,710
Then he shouldn't have gotten married
in the first place!

423
00:22:35,793 --> 00:22:36,794
Oh, Mom.

424
00:22:39,130 --> 00:22:41,632
Call me shallow if you want,
but I can't help it.

425
00:22:42,717 --> 00:22:46,012
Thing is, I want my daughter
to walk on a paved road.

426
00:22:46,512 --> 00:22:49,140
I don't want her tripping
over rocks in life.

427
00:22:49,891 --> 00:22:51,184
So I don't approve.

428
00:22:53,227 --> 00:22:55,229
[gentle music playing]

429
00:22:59,817 --> 00:23:00,818
[sighs]

430
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:08,492
We knew this would happen.

431
00:23:08,993 --> 00:23:12,580
I know, but I didn't think
she'd be so strongly against it.

432
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,498
I understand her.

433
00:23:14,582 --> 00:23:17,001
It's only natural
she thinks I'm not good enough.

434
00:23:17,084 --> 00:23:20,630
[sighs] Yeah. She just cares about me.

435
00:23:22,632 --> 00:23:24,592
[sighs] It's okay, though.

436
00:23:25,134 --> 00:23:28,638
No matter what my mom says,
I'm still going to keep seeing you.

437
00:23:29,513 --> 00:23:31,224
So don't let it get to you either.

438
00:23:31,307 --> 00:23:33,768
We're both in this for marriage after all.

439
00:23:34,268 --> 00:23:36,896
So even if it takes time,
we need to get her blessing.

440
00:23:38,231 --> 00:23:39,398
Yeah, but how?

441
00:23:41,484 --> 00:23:44,362
Why don't you do things your way,
and I'll do them my way?

442
00:23:44,862 --> 00:23:46,113
One step at a time.

443
00:23:47,782 --> 00:23:50,534
-[courier] Are you Ms. Nam Hye-gyeong?
-Yes, that's me.

444
00:23:50,618 --> 00:23:51,786
[courier] Delivery for you.

445
00:23:51,869 --> 00:23:52,870
PREMIUM 6-YEAR
KOREAN RED GINSENG

446
00:23:52,954 --> 00:23:55,206
Um… [sighs] Red ginseng?

447
00:23:55,289 --> 00:23:57,375
But who sent this?

448
00:23:58,042 --> 00:24:01,087
-Uh, it was sent anonymously, ma'am.
-Oh. [chuckles]

449
00:24:01,712 --> 00:24:03,005
Thank you so much.

450
00:24:11,013 --> 00:24:12,598
[sighs]

451
00:24:16,978 --> 00:24:19,313
[Si-woo] What are you doing here
so early in the morning?

452
00:24:19,397 --> 00:24:22,149
Well, what else? I'm here to work out.

453
00:24:22,942 --> 00:24:25,236
Let's do it together.
You're our key asset.

454
00:24:29,490 --> 00:24:30,741
Do you play any golf?

455
00:24:31,575 --> 00:24:32,827
I don't like golf.

456
00:24:33,703 --> 00:24:34,787
That won't do.

457
00:24:35,288 --> 00:24:37,873
You should start now
if you want to become an executive.

458
00:24:38,374 --> 00:24:42,211
I have a private coach,
so maybe we could take lessons toge…

459
00:24:42,295 --> 00:24:43,337
Wait.

460
00:24:44,505 --> 00:24:45,756
Whoa!

461
00:24:45,840 --> 00:24:48,592
That won't be happening, sir.
Please, just get to the point.

462
00:24:48,676 --> 00:24:50,553
Are you serious about leaving the company?

463
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:52,346
Yes.

464
00:24:52,430 --> 00:24:54,765
I have a rough idea
of why you're doing this,

465
00:24:54,849 --> 00:24:57,810
but you should think of President Han.
She thinks the world of you.

466
00:24:59,854 --> 00:25:03,190
It's a little ridiculous
hearing you worry about President Han.

467
00:25:03,274 --> 00:25:06,027
-[sighs]
-Don't worry.

468
00:25:06,110 --> 00:25:08,654
I'm sure she'll be perfectly fine
without me.

469
00:25:13,075 --> 00:25:14,201
Hey, Kang Si-woo.

470
00:25:15,828 --> 00:25:17,246
[groans] Really?

471
00:25:17,913 --> 00:25:19,790
[clears throat] Uh… [chuckles]

472
00:25:19,874 --> 00:25:21,459
Since the team lead position is vacant,

473
00:25:21,542 --> 00:25:24,962
I'll temporarily be stepping in
as the acting team lead. [chuckles]

474
00:25:25,046 --> 00:25:27,840
Um, so you can all just keep doing
what you've been doing, all right?

475
00:25:27,923 --> 00:25:29,300
[workers] Yes, sir.

476
00:25:29,383 --> 00:25:31,093
-[applause]
-Oh, please.

477
00:25:32,553 --> 00:25:35,598
Ah, Ms. No-ah, if you could hand over
your duties to Ms. Cha before you leave.

478
00:25:35,681 --> 00:25:36,515
Sure.

479
00:25:36,599 --> 00:25:38,142
Also, a new hire is starting today.

480
00:25:38,225 --> 00:25:39,769
Can someone mentor him, please?

481
00:25:44,273 --> 00:25:45,399
[chuckles]

482
00:25:45,900 --> 00:25:47,360
Uh, anyone at all?

483
00:25:48,569 --> 00:25:50,363
Oh. Here he comes.

484
00:25:53,491 --> 00:25:55,493
[dreamy music playing]

485
00:26:07,046 --> 00:26:07,880
Hello, everyone.

486
00:26:08,464 --> 00:26:10,091
I'm the new hire, Song Min-gyu.

487
00:26:12,676 --> 00:26:14,261
Uh, I will, sir.

488
00:26:15,304 --> 00:26:16,305
[chuckles]

489
00:26:20,768 --> 00:26:21,769
Thank you, sir.

490
00:26:30,277 --> 00:26:32,196
Even Ms. Na-ri returned to her old team.

491
00:26:32,696 --> 00:26:35,282
But have you still not decided yet?

492
00:26:35,366 --> 00:26:36,492
Uh, well, um…

493
00:26:36,992 --> 00:26:40,579
I was planning to decide
after seeing where you go first.

494
00:26:40,663 --> 00:26:41,789
Are you planning to follow me?

495
00:26:42,415 --> 00:26:43,499
Yeah. [chuckles]

496
00:26:47,169 --> 00:26:48,337
I intend to resign.

497
00:26:48,421 --> 00:26:49,713
Oh. [chuckles]

498
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:52,007
What?

499
00:26:52,091 --> 00:26:53,968
So don't wait for me
and make your own decision.

500
00:26:54,552 --> 00:26:55,553
But why?

501
00:26:55,636 --> 00:26:58,389
Well, I just want to look for work
that suits me better.

502
00:26:59,014 --> 00:27:01,016
I hope you'll take
this chance to do the same.

503
00:27:01,725 --> 00:27:04,520
But working under you
is what really suits me best.

504
00:27:08,190 --> 00:27:09,316
And the Development Team?

505
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:12,153
You enjoy development work
more than the actual planning stage.

506
00:27:12,236 --> 00:27:15,573
Yeah, that's true,
but going to Development now is a bit…

507
00:27:15,656 --> 00:27:18,159
The response to your washer-dryer
has been great.

508
00:27:18,701 --> 00:27:21,829
So everyone will understand
if you choose to make the move.

509
00:27:22,997 --> 00:27:23,998
Yeah. [chuckles]

510
00:27:24,665 --> 00:27:26,083
I'll transfer there, then.

511
00:27:26,167 --> 00:27:28,419
So I'll go ahead
and speak to their team lead.

512
00:27:29,003 --> 00:27:30,129
In return,

513
00:27:30,212 --> 00:27:32,923
please keep my resignation
a secret for the time being.

514
00:27:34,758 --> 00:27:36,302
Man, it's a real shame. [sighs]

515
00:27:36,385 --> 00:27:38,512
Though I'm sure you'll end up
somewhere better.

516
00:27:40,473 --> 00:27:41,724
Yeah.

517
00:27:42,766 --> 00:27:44,852
I'll be sure to end up somewhere better.

518
00:27:47,938 --> 00:27:51,108
-[Ji-yoon chuckling] Exactly.
-[Min-gyu chuckles]

519
00:27:51,192 --> 00:27:52,526
Oh, Mr. Kang!

520
00:27:54,528 --> 00:27:56,030
This is our new hire.

521
00:27:56,113 --> 00:27:57,615
This is Manager Kang Si-woo.

522
00:27:57,698 --> 00:28:01,243
Oh… Nice to meet you, sir.
My name is Song Min-gyu.

523
00:28:02,119 --> 00:28:03,120
Okay.

524
00:28:04,288 --> 00:28:06,207
[Kee-tae] I think you came
to the wrong place.

525
00:28:06,790 --> 00:28:09,084
You don't look like you work
in electronics. [chuckling]

526
00:28:09,668 --> 00:28:10,836
Ah…

527
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:13,589
Many people tell me
I look like a movie star.

528
00:28:14,215 --> 00:28:17,218
-O-Oh, confident. [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

529
00:28:17,301 --> 00:28:19,428
Min-gyu, what would you like to drink?

530
00:28:19,512 --> 00:28:21,722
-Do you like instant coffee?
-Oh.

531
00:28:21,805 --> 00:28:24,600
If your mentor offers you coffee,
you should say no.

532
00:28:26,310 --> 00:28:27,937
Uh, just a moment.

533
00:28:29,104 --> 00:28:31,148
"Say no to instant coffee."

534
00:28:31,232 --> 00:28:32,316
CHECKLIST
NO TO INSTANT COFFEE

535
00:28:32,399 --> 00:28:33,651
Understood, sir.

536
00:28:33,734 --> 00:28:36,195
And say no if she tries to lure you out
for chicken and beer.

537
00:28:36,278 --> 00:28:37,404
Oh.

538
00:28:37,488 --> 00:28:39,532
"Say no to fried chicken and beer."

539
00:28:39,615 --> 00:28:41,116
-[scoffing]
-[Si-woo] And for the record,

540
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:43,452
Ms. Cha Ji-yoon already has a boyfriend.

541
00:28:44,328 --> 00:28:46,956
"She has a boyfr…"

542
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:49,041
[chuckles]

543
00:28:52,670 --> 00:28:54,922
Oh. [chuckles]

544
00:28:55,005 --> 00:28:56,006
I'll keep that in mind.

545
00:28:57,341 --> 00:28:58,342
You're very lucky

546
00:28:58,425 --> 00:29:00,803
for landing a great mentor
from the beginning.

547
00:29:05,391 --> 00:29:06,225
Indeed.

548
00:29:08,769 --> 00:29:10,563
[doorbell rings]

549
00:29:12,189 --> 00:29:13,524
[Hye-gyeong chuckles]

550
00:29:14,191 --> 00:29:15,818
What is it this time?

551
00:29:15,901 --> 00:29:17,778
It says health supplements.

552
00:29:20,447 --> 00:29:21,490
Thank you.

553
00:29:32,501 --> 00:29:33,502
Oh, gosh.

554
00:29:33,586 --> 00:29:36,422
PREMIUM MULTIVITAMIN FOR WOMEN
COGNITIVE CARE

555
00:29:36,505 --> 00:29:38,841
RECIPIENT: MS. NAM HYE-GYEONG

556
00:29:44,597 --> 00:29:45,723
[sighs]

557
00:29:45,806 --> 00:29:51,020
[somber music playing]

558
00:29:55,024 --> 00:29:56,150
[sighs]

559
00:29:58,611 --> 00:30:02,364
[No-ah] Look, if you don't respect me,
then I won't respect you either.

560
00:30:03,991 --> 00:30:04,992
[Jae-in] Mmm.

561
00:30:05,743 --> 00:30:09,371
[No-ah] In a relationship,
I'm still going to put myself first.

562
00:30:10,039 --> 00:30:10,873
[Jae-in] Mmm.

563
00:30:10,956 --> 00:30:12,708
If your love fades away…

564
00:30:13,292 --> 00:30:15,044
I will leave without forgiving you.

565
00:30:16,712 --> 00:30:17,588
[Jae-in] Mmm.

566
00:30:18,589 --> 00:30:20,174
[No-ah] That's how I'll love you.

567
00:30:21,425 --> 00:30:23,093
I hope you'll do the same for me.

568
00:30:25,554 --> 00:30:26,388
[Jae-in] Mmm.

569
00:30:26,472 --> 00:30:27,890
It's the first time

570
00:30:27,973 --> 00:30:29,725
I'm recognized purely
for my own hard work.

571
00:30:30,601 --> 00:30:32,269
Even if I do end up with you,

572
00:30:32,353 --> 00:30:34,688
I want to be
a better version of myself first.

573
00:30:35,522 --> 00:30:39,026
But before being Lee Jae-in's girlfriend,

574
00:30:40,235 --> 00:30:41,654
I wanna be Yoon No-ah first.

575
00:30:43,113 --> 00:30:44,698
I don't know if I can either.

576
00:30:45,449 --> 00:30:49,203
The thing is… I can't bear the thought
of ever losing you.

577
00:31:07,638 --> 00:31:08,764
No-ah.

578
00:31:10,432 --> 00:31:12,685
Kim Goo-won? What are you doing here?

579
00:31:15,979 --> 00:31:18,607
I can't take it anymore.
Let's get back together.

580
00:31:19,650 --> 00:31:21,402
What the hell are you doing?

581
00:31:23,445 --> 00:31:25,614
I heard that you're still going out
with that kid.

582
00:31:26,699 --> 00:31:30,369
Snap out of it, Yoon Noah.
Why are you ruining yourself over me?

583
00:31:31,412 --> 00:31:32,955
You fought with your girlfriend?

584
00:31:33,038 --> 00:31:34,998
[sighs] I'm going to end things
with her soon.

585
00:31:35,082 --> 00:31:36,709
You haven't changed a bit.

586
00:31:37,793 --> 00:31:39,503
You piece of trash.

587
00:31:41,630 --> 00:31:44,341
Look at yourself.
Do you realize how much you've changed?

588
00:31:45,092 --> 00:31:46,719
You're not the Yoon No-ah I used to know.

589
00:31:46,802 --> 00:31:49,179
Yeah, I've changed a lot!

590
00:31:49,263 --> 00:31:52,766
I've become more selfish
and more courageous than ever.

591
00:31:54,226 --> 00:31:56,061
So please,
just get the hell out of my life.

592
00:31:57,146 --> 00:31:59,940
No-ah, you know that you need me.

593
00:32:00,023 --> 00:32:01,942
[sighs] Let go.

594
00:32:03,318 --> 00:32:05,237
I said let go!

595
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:06,155
Stop!

596
00:32:09,199 --> 00:32:10,159
She told you to let go.

597
00:32:12,161 --> 00:32:13,412
You need to get lost.

598
00:32:13,495 --> 00:32:15,038
And you better stop
following No-ah around.

599
00:32:15,122 --> 00:32:17,082
I'm not following her around. I love her.

600
00:32:17,666 --> 00:32:19,126
[Goo-won scoffs] You love her?

601
00:32:19,209 --> 00:32:21,670
What do you even know
about No-ah to call it love?

602
00:32:21,754 --> 00:32:23,297
I certainly know her better than you.

603
00:32:24,006 --> 00:32:26,091
I know what an amazing person she is.

604
00:32:32,639 --> 00:32:34,975
Kim Goo-won, listen carefully.

605
00:32:35,058 --> 00:32:37,102
Jae-in is the man that I love.

606
00:32:38,020 --> 00:32:39,688
So don't ever show your face again.

607
00:32:39,772 --> 00:32:41,440
I'll call the police if you do.

608
00:32:42,983 --> 00:32:45,819
Just don't come running back to me later,
crying and begging.

609
00:32:54,495 --> 00:32:55,662
[sighs]

610
00:32:59,625 --> 00:33:00,793
Listen, Jae-in.

611
00:33:03,295 --> 00:33:06,965
I can't promise that
I'll wait for you until you get back.

612
00:33:08,509 --> 00:33:09,676
Are you still okay with that?

613
00:33:11,470 --> 00:33:12,805
[chuckles]

614
00:33:14,723 --> 00:33:18,727
If either of us finds it too hard,
we end it right then and there.

615
00:33:19,978 --> 00:33:20,979
Is that okay?

616
00:33:22,648 --> 00:33:23,774
Mmm.

617
00:33:23,857 --> 00:33:25,484
But I know that I can handle it.

618
00:33:27,569 --> 00:33:28,779
I told you before.

619
00:33:29,446 --> 00:33:31,615
Love's not about holding back
or forcing things.

620
00:33:31,698 --> 00:33:33,158
I won't hold back.

621
00:33:33,242 --> 00:33:35,994
I'll video call you every day,
I'll write you letters,

622
00:33:36,078 --> 00:33:38,288
and fly back at least twice a year.

623
00:33:38,372 --> 00:33:40,874
I'll meet you halfway
in some random country

624
00:33:40,958 --> 00:33:42,501
if that's what it takes.

625
00:33:52,469 --> 00:33:54,596
We should see each other more
before you leave.

626
00:33:57,349 --> 00:33:58,350
Mmm.

627
00:34:00,769 --> 00:34:02,563
[giggles]

628
00:34:09,695 --> 00:34:11,071
What are you doing here?

629
00:34:14,366 --> 00:34:15,659
Hello, Mother.

630
00:34:15,742 --> 00:34:18,120
I'd prefer if you didn't call me that.

631
00:34:19,663 --> 00:34:20,914
I asked what are you doing here?

632
00:34:20,998 --> 00:34:25,377
Well, whenever I need to clear my head,
I come here and help out Mr. Cha.

633
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:28,881
I'm confused.

634
00:34:28,964 --> 00:34:31,258
Doesn't one typically send
flowers or fruit baskets

635
00:34:31,341 --> 00:34:32,885
when trying to win someone over?

636
00:34:33,468 --> 00:34:36,346
You think I'm some fragile old lady?
Sending me all that bitter stuff.

637
00:34:36,430 --> 00:34:38,849
I don't want the people
I care about to get sick.

638
00:34:41,727 --> 00:34:44,980
Then, do you give
my Ji-yoon gifts like that too?

639
00:34:45,564 --> 00:34:46,773
[chuckles] Yes.

640
00:34:46,857 --> 00:34:50,277
Men are all the same.
You don't get what women actually want.

641
00:34:52,112 --> 00:34:53,947
So, how long
were you going to send me those?

642
00:34:54,031 --> 00:34:56,325
Until you called me and told me to stop.

643
00:34:57,242 --> 00:34:59,202
I didn't want to show up
and make you uneasy,

644
00:34:59,286 --> 00:35:00,287
so I just waited.

645
00:35:01,371 --> 00:35:03,248
The ship might sail while you wait.

646
00:35:04,458 --> 00:35:07,085
Anyway, try fixing this. It won't turn on.

647
00:35:08,045 --> 00:35:09,046
Sure.

648
00:35:26,438 --> 00:35:28,398
That back looks so familiar.

649
00:35:32,694 --> 00:35:34,279
What do you like about my Ji-yoon, huh?

650
00:35:34,363 --> 00:35:35,364
[clicks]

651
00:35:41,078 --> 00:35:45,499
I really admire her confidence
and her strong sense of responsibility.

652
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:49,002
She makes discoveries
others don't even consider.

653
00:35:49,086 --> 00:35:50,253
And once she sets a goal,

654
00:35:50,337 --> 00:35:52,422
she gives it her all
until she's satisfied.

655
00:35:53,382 --> 00:35:55,634
And Ji-yoon, unlike myself,

656
00:35:55,717 --> 00:35:58,553
she knows how to open up
and share her feelings.

657
00:35:59,554 --> 00:36:00,889
I'm learning a lot from her.

658
00:36:01,932 --> 00:36:04,017
You could go on all night, couldn't you?

659
00:36:04,101 --> 00:36:07,437
I could talk all night
about the reasons I fell in love with her.

660
00:36:10,232 --> 00:36:11,900
[chuckles]

661
00:36:13,485 --> 00:36:15,195
-All fixed.
-Already?

662
00:36:15,862 --> 00:36:18,323
If it was this simple,
why couldn't my husband fix it?

663
00:36:19,032 --> 00:36:20,283
Oh my, what's this?

664
00:36:22,244 --> 00:36:24,037
I got the feeling you liked flowers.

665
00:36:24,705 --> 00:36:25,747
[chuckles]

666
00:36:30,669 --> 00:36:31,837
Mr. Kang, I…

667
00:36:32,796 --> 00:36:33,839
Mom.

668
00:36:33,922 --> 00:36:35,799
So you've been meeting here
behind my back?

669
00:36:36,883 --> 00:36:40,303
No, this… this isn't what it looks like.
I just ran into Ji-Yoon.

670
00:36:43,598 --> 00:36:45,517
I got some bungeoppang. Your favorite.

671
00:36:45,600 --> 00:36:46,977
Now, why would you do that?

672
00:36:48,478 --> 00:36:50,188
He beat you with the kindness.

673
00:36:52,983 --> 00:36:54,192
Right.

674
00:36:54,276 --> 00:36:57,279
A major corporation
beats a tiny corner store.

675
00:36:59,364 --> 00:37:02,075
Working at SAEUM is the one thing
I like about you.

676
00:37:03,785 --> 00:37:05,162
Well, about that…

677
00:37:05,245 --> 00:37:07,706
I'm planning to resign from SAEUM.

678
00:37:09,583 --> 00:37:12,711
[stammers] Well, you know, I'm sure
he was headhunted by a better company.

679
00:37:12,794 --> 00:37:13,712
[chuckles] Right?

680
00:37:14,963 --> 00:37:16,173
I intend to take a break

681
00:37:16,256 --> 00:37:18,008
while I figure out my next steps in life.

682
00:37:18,091 --> 00:37:20,510
[Hye-gyeong] You're walking away
from the one thing I like about you?

683
00:37:20,594 --> 00:37:21,762
[groans] Forget it.

684
00:37:21,845 --> 00:37:23,972
A divorce is one thing, but unemployed?

685
00:37:24,056 --> 00:37:25,140
-No way.
-Mom.

686
00:37:26,641 --> 00:37:28,810
-Mom, come on.
-Oh, gosh. Hang on.

687
00:37:29,644 --> 00:37:30,812
-[sighs]
-Mom!

688
00:37:40,322 --> 00:37:43,408
Hey. Why'd you bring that up
when things were going so well?

689
00:37:43,492 --> 00:37:45,619
She'd be angrier if she found out later.

690
00:37:45,702 --> 00:37:48,163
Good grief, you really are frustrating.

691
00:37:48,789 --> 00:37:51,625
I thought long and hard
about how to convince you,

692
00:37:52,709 --> 00:37:54,419
but it boiled down to one thing.

693
00:37:55,003 --> 00:37:56,046
I like…

694
00:37:57,214 --> 00:37:58,423
that man…

695
00:37:59,966 --> 00:38:01,218
very much.

696
00:38:02,677 --> 00:38:05,097
First he gave up on his marriage,
now his career.

697
00:38:05,180 --> 00:38:06,723
How can I trust or like him?

698
00:38:06,807 --> 00:38:08,183
But I trust him.

699
00:38:08,850 --> 00:38:13,146
He's the only one
who lets me be myself completely, Mom.

700
00:38:13,688 --> 00:38:17,359
So I know that he'll find a job
that lets him be himself too.

701
00:38:19,111 --> 00:38:21,780
Even his personality
is just like your dad's.

702
00:38:22,823 --> 00:38:24,741
There isn't a single thing
I like about him.

703
00:38:25,617 --> 00:38:27,869
I guess in the end I do take after you.

704
00:38:28,453 --> 00:38:30,080
You don't take after me.

705
00:38:31,748 --> 00:38:34,793
You're far smarter than me
and more upstanding than me.

706
00:38:37,921 --> 00:38:40,048
You've always been my pride and joy.

707
00:38:42,884 --> 00:38:45,387
I'm sorry, Mom.

708
00:38:47,139 --> 00:38:48,390
[sighs]

709
00:38:54,312 --> 00:38:58,108
I guess we've overcome one hurdle.

710
00:38:59,025 --> 00:39:00,986
And how did you reach that conclusion?

711
00:39:01,486 --> 00:39:04,114
She said, "A divorce is one thing."

712
00:39:04,197 --> 00:39:06,158
So that means
she's softened up a little bit.

713
00:39:06,241 --> 00:39:08,201
She also called me a bum.

714
00:39:08,285 --> 00:39:11,788
Oh, come on.
You'll get that sorted out soon enough.

715
00:39:13,165 --> 00:39:15,208
It might take quite a while, though.

716
00:39:15,292 --> 00:39:18,295
Hmm. Guess I'll have to be
the breadwinner, then.

717
00:39:20,463 --> 00:39:23,175
Tomorrow will be my last day at work.

718
00:39:26,386 --> 00:39:28,221
-Tomorrow?
-Yes.

719
00:39:28,722 --> 00:39:31,558
I'll submit my resignation
and use my paid leave.

720
00:39:32,142 --> 00:39:35,812
[sighs] So your final day
has actually arrived.

721
00:39:35,896 --> 00:39:38,857
Ji-yoon, you'll root for me
as a colleague now, right?

722
00:39:39,524 --> 00:39:42,152
It's a shame, but yes.

723
00:39:51,328 --> 00:39:54,080
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
NAME: KANG SI-WOO

724
00:39:55,832 --> 00:39:57,375
[Ji-yoon] But it feels like a waste

725
00:39:57,459 --> 00:40:00,295
to throw away everything you've built
over the years,

726
00:40:00,962 --> 00:40:02,797
and everything that would've followed.

727
00:40:02,881 --> 00:40:03,882
Think it over again.

728
00:40:03,965 --> 00:40:06,593
I can't work the way I do now
under any other boss.

729
00:40:06,676 --> 00:40:10,805
Can't you just stay on
as our boss, Mr. Kang?

730
00:40:18,188 --> 00:40:20,023
CONFIRM SUBMISSION
WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEND THE FORM?

731
00:40:20,106 --> 00:40:20,941
CONFIRM

732
00:40:21,024 --> 00:40:22,567
SENT

733
00:40:27,530 --> 00:40:28,531
[knocks]

734
00:40:36,039 --> 00:40:38,166
I take it Mr. Noh didn't exactly deliver.

735
00:40:38,250 --> 00:40:39,918
But you already knew that he couldn't.

736
00:40:43,171 --> 00:40:47,217
Well, if I can't keep you here,
I'll leave them with a massive liability.

737
00:40:47,300 --> 00:40:49,886
Which is why you put my status
as a key asset on the table.

738
00:40:49,970 --> 00:40:51,137
Yes.

739
00:40:52,180 --> 00:40:53,723
It's not too late to change your mind.

740
00:40:53,807 --> 00:40:54,849
Thank you.

741
00:40:55,433 --> 00:40:58,186
But I won't be able to give you
the support you expect from me.

742
00:40:58,270 --> 00:40:59,562
[sighs]

743
00:40:59,646 --> 00:41:00,647
But here…

744
00:41:05,694 --> 00:41:06,820
What's this?

745
00:41:06,903 --> 00:41:08,196
You'll find it helpful.

746
00:41:08,780 --> 00:41:11,449
[Hyeon-u] Here's what you asked me about.

747
00:41:12,033 --> 00:41:13,451
Your hunch was spot on.

748
00:41:13,535 --> 00:41:16,955
Turns out the subcontractors
were treating Mr. Noh and Mr. Ko

749
00:41:17,038 --> 00:41:19,457
to rounds of golf to sell their products.

750
00:41:19,541 --> 00:41:21,293
And it's true,
those two have been bragging

751
00:41:21,376 --> 00:41:23,336
about taking over the Home-AI project.

752
00:41:24,587 --> 00:41:26,047
Here's all their expense reports.

753
00:41:27,465 --> 00:41:28,466
[Si-woo sighs]

754
00:41:30,010 --> 00:41:31,011
Thank you.

755
00:41:31,720 --> 00:41:34,055
It seems like the Vice President
is involved too.

756
00:41:34,139 --> 00:41:35,515
You sure this is okay?

757
00:41:37,726 --> 00:41:38,810
Mmm.

758
00:41:38,893 --> 00:41:41,146
Right now,
it's just the subcontractors' word,

759
00:41:41,229 --> 00:41:42,981
so you'll need to verify the facts.

760
00:41:43,815 --> 00:41:47,110
I'll leave it up to you
to decide how you want to play this.

761
00:41:52,282 --> 00:41:54,659
So you're leaving me a bomb
as a parting gift?

762
00:41:56,953 --> 00:42:00,582
There's no changing your mind
at this point, is there?

763
00:42:00,665 --> 00:42:01,499
No.

764
00:42:02,876 --> 00:42:04,461
I wouldn't have made it here without you.

765
00:42:04,544 --> 00:42:06,838
[soft pop music playing]

766
00:42:06,921 --> 00:42:08,673
You got here on your own merit.

767
00:42:08,757 --> 00:42:12,260
I look forward to seeing
Kang Si-woo's next chapter.

768
00:42:12,761 --> 00:42:13,762
Thank you, ma'am.

769
00:42:17,265 --> 00:42:20,060
This is your noncompete agreement.

770
00:42:21,353 --> 00:42:24,356
It stipulates that you cannot work
in the same industry

771
00:42:24,439 --> 00:42:26,316
for one year post termination.

772
00:42:28,068 --> 00:42:29,069
Okay.

773
00:42:33,573 --> 00:42:35,241
I haven't even approved
the resignation yet,

774
00:42:35,325 --> 00:42:36,743
so what do you think you're doing?

775
00:42:36,826 --> 00:42:38,745
-President Han has approved it.
-What?

776
00:42:38,828 --> 00:42:41,081
Her instructions were
to skip the exit interview

777
00:42:41,164 --> 00:42:42,457
and wrap this up quickly.

778
00:42:44,709 --> 00:42:46,127
[Noh sighs]

779
00:42:47,587 --> 00:42:52,801
SIGNATORY: KANG SI-WOO

780
00:42:57,472 --> 00:42:59,391
Thank you for all your hard work.

781
00:42:59,974 --> 00:43:02,352
Thank you. I will be signing off now.

782
00:43:02,435 --> 00:43:05,939
TASK FORCE MANAGER
KANG SI-WOO

783
00:43:15,990 --> 00:43:17,242
[rapid footsteps approaching]

784
00:43:17,325 --> 00:43:18,785
Mr. Kang!

785
00:43:19,661 --> 00:43:22,997
Ms. Cha is in the product showroom
right now, and… [pants]

786
00:43:24,499 --> 00:43:25,583
Mr. Kang!

787
00:43:31,214 --> 00:43:33,049
Huh? Why are you here so early?

788
00:43:33,633 --> 00:43:34,801
Whoa, he's super fast!

789
00:43:34,884 --> 00:43:37,637
Hey, you should've brought him
right on time, you dummy.

790
00:43:37,720 --> 00:43:38,847
I know, but…

791
00:43:38,930 --> 00:43:43,017
I was literally trying to say Ms. Cha
was waiting in the product showroom,

792
00:43:43,643 --> 00:43:46,020
but he just bolted off
before I could even finish!

793
00:43:46,104 --> 00:43:49,941
Did you think she was in
some kind of trouble, Mr. Kang? [giggles]

794
00:43:50,024 --> 00:43:52,569
Either way, I've never seen
Kang Si-woo run so fast.

795
00:43:52,652 --> 00:43:54,320
[laughing]

796
00:43:54,404 --> 00:43:56,614
What are you all gathered here for?

797
00:43:56,698 --> 00:43:58,491
They're tearing down this setup soon.

798
00:43:58,575 --> 00:44:01,202
That's why Mr. Kim suggested
we run one final test.

799
00:44:01,286 --> 00:44:02,287
A test?

800
00:44:02,370 --> 00:44:04,247
You should at least do a final check

801
00:44:04,330 --> 00:44:07,459
to make sure our launched products
don't have any issues before you leave.

802
00:44:07,542 --> 00:44:09,252
-[bell dings]
-Ready. All right…

803
00:44:10,628 --> 00:44:12,130
[door opens]

804
00:44:14,841 --> 00:44:17,135
-[Kee-tae] That's right.
-[staff cheering]

805
00:44:17,218 --> 00:44:20,305
This was the exact moment
you were supposed to bring him in

806
00:44:20,388 --> 00:44:22,265
so that we can…

807
00:44:22,348 --> 00:44:24,017
-[party cracker pops]
-[cheering]

808
00:44:24,100 --> 00:44:26,853
-Congratulations on your resignation!
-Congratulations on resigning!

809
00:44:27,353 --> 00:44:28,605
Congratulations.

810
00:44:30,023 --> 00:44:32,859
At least let us throw you
a farewell party.

811
00:44:32,942 --> 00:44:34,944
[Na-ri] How could you, Mr. Kang?

812
00:44:35,028 --> 00:44:37,822
I was the last to find out again.

813
00:44:39,741 --> 00:44:40,742
I'm sorry.

814
00:44:46,789 --> 00:44:49,459
Mr. Kang,
did you just apologize with a smile?

815
00:44:49,542 --> 00:44:52,045
Then "No sorries" no longer applies,
neither does "No smiles."

816
00:44:52,128 --> 00:44:54,547
And look, there are "people" all around.

817
00:44:54,631 --> 00:44:56,633
You're officially no longer Three-No-Man.

818
00:44:58,301 --> 00:44:59,302
Right.

819
00:44:59,886 --> 00:45:02,263
Now that I'm leaving, I can finally

820
00:45:02,931 --> 00:45:05,350
appreciate the reasons
why I should have stayed.

821
00:45:06,643 --> 00:45:10,146
Only today did I learn
what makes work truly worthwhile.

822
00:45:11,147 --> 00:45:13,900
You all were my reason,
and made it worthwhile.

823
00:45:14,776 --> 00:45:16,027
Thank you all

824
00:45:17,237 --> 00:45:18,321
for everything.

825
00:45:32,085 --> 00:45:34,087
Well, now, now, now.

826
00:45:34,921 --> 00:45:36,381
-Ta-da!
-[Kee-tae] Wow!

827
00:45:37,048 --> 00:45:39,467
It's not a farewell party
unless there's a toast.

828
00:45:39,551 --> 00:45:41,386
[chuckles] Let me pour you a drink.

829
00:45:46,266 --> 00:45:48,560
You're Kang Si-woo after all.
You'll do great anywhere.

830
00:45:49,561 --> 00:45:50,562
Thank you so much.

831
00:45:50,645 --> 00:45:52,105
[chuckles] Here.

832
00:45:52,730 --> 00:45:56,359
But man, the office is going to feel
so empty once you leave too, No-ah.

833
00:45:56,943 --> 00:45:59,153
[chuckles]
I'll be back before you know it.

834
00:45:59,237 --> 00:46:00,280
Of course.

835
00:46:02,198 --> 00:46:03,366
[chuckles]

836
00:46:05,410 --> 00:46:07,870
[Mr. Kim] Yeah, just a little for me. Yes.

837
00:46:07,954 --> 00:46:08,955
[chuckles]

838
00:46:10,498 --> 00:46:12,458
[Mr. Kim] All right,
everyone has a drink, right?

839
00:46:12,542 --> 00:46:15,003
Now, Sr. Associate Kee-tae,
can you give us a killer toast?

840
00:46:15,086 --> 00:46:17,130
[Kee-tae] Right, uh… [sighs]

841
00:46:17,213 --> 00:46:21,259
Mr. Kang Si-woo,
I hope that wherever you go,

842
00:46:21,759 --> 00:46:25,471
you spread your notorious reputation
far and wide.

843
00:46:25,555 --> 00:46:27,515
[chuckles] And now,
everybody, let's cheers!

844
00:46:27,599 --> 00:46:28,600
Cheers, guys!

845
00:46:28,683 --> 00:46:30,685
[all] Cheers!

846
00:46:30,768 --> 00:46:33,771
[upbeat music playing]

847
00:47:23,112 --> 00:47:26,240
NO SCHEDULED EVENTS TODAY

848
00:47:45,760 --> 00:47:46,886
I'm sorry, ma'am.

849
00:47:46,969 --> 00:47:50,848
[sighs] So you're saying
you sent out that half-baked report

850
00:47:51,432 --> 00:47:54,560
and actually cc'd the managing director,
too, on the email?

851
00:47:55,353 --> 00:47:57,438
I thought I had to send it to everyone.

852
00:47:57,522 --> 00:47:58,564
[sighs]

853
00:47:59,982 --> 00:48:04,153
I'm pretty sure that I sent you
a detailed guide on email etiquette.

854
00:48:04,237 --> 00:48:05,613
I'm sorry, ma'am.

855
00:48:06,280 --> 00:48:08,074
I haven't fully memorized it yet.

856
00:48:08,616 --> 00:48:09,867
Drink this.

857
00:48:12,954 --> 00:48:16,165
They say chamomile helps
when you're tense and nervous.

858
00:48:24,924 --> 00:48:25,925
Thank you, ma'am.

859
00:48:27,385 --> 00:48:31,889
I accidentally dropped a zero
from every number once

860
00:48:31,973 --> 00:48:34,726
in a simulation of profit and loss.

861
00:48:36,102 --> 00:48:39,939
So that means $100 became 10.

862
00:48:40,022 --> 00:48:42,608
Wow, it sounds like you got an earful.

863
00:48:42,692 --> 00:48:44,444
What was it he said?

864
00:48:45,528 --> 00:48:47,739
"Making one mistake is more than enough."

865
00:48:47,822 --> 00:48:49,741
Repeated mistakes are not mistakes.

866
00:48:49,824 --> 00:48:51,451
It shows their lack of competence.

867
00:48:52,326 --> 00:48:54,662
I'm disappointed in you, Ms. Cha.

868
00:48:56,414 --> 00:48:57,582
[sighs]

869
00:48:57,665 --> 00:48:59,417
Just hearing you gives me the chills.

870
00:49:00,668 --> 00:49:01,878
But still,

871
00:49:03,254 --> 00:49:05,757
I genuinely learned so much
from him, you know?

872
00:49:09,844 --> 00:49:12,680
He also taught me
what it means to be a colleague.

873
00:49:13,431 --> 00:49:14,891
If you say that I am,

874
00:49:15,558 --> 00:49:16,768
it must be true.

875
00:49:18,352 --> 00:49:19,645
He also taught me…

876
00:49:21,606 --> 00:49:24,233
how to put my own well-being first.

877
00:49:24,317 --> 00:49:26,235
I warned you about junk food.

878
00:49:26,319 --> 00:49:28,321
The coffee and sugary drinks!

879
00:49:30,198 --> 00:49:32,325
He told me, "Forget sacrifice bunts,

880
00:49:34,285 --> 00:49:36,162
and become a hero instead of that."

881
00:49:39,957 --> 00:49:42,293
[exhales deeply]

882
00:49:43,211 --> 00:49:45,087
And he taught me how to

883
00:49:46,214 --> 00:49:48,758
fight back against any unfair treatment.

884
00:49:48,841 --> 00:49:49,759
[Si-woo] Besides,

885
00:49:50,343 --> 00:49:53,554
that word carries more weight
the more sparingly you say it.

886
00:49:54,305 --> 00:49:56,516
Please don't say that
when you're around me.

887
00:49:57,016 --> 00:49:58,017
Especially at work.

888
00:49:58,935 --> 00:50:00,812
Well, he actually taught me…

889
00:50:02,605 --> 00:50:04,565
everything that I need to know.

890
00:50:05,566 --> 00:50:09,111
[gentle music playing]

891
00:50:11,864 --> 00:50:12,990
[sniffles]

892
00:50:14,492 --> 00:50:16,452
Wait, why are you suddenly…

893
00:50:16,536 --> 00:50:18,538
[crying]

894
00:50:21,123 --> 00:50:23,125
[sobbing]

895
00:50:35,137 --> 00:50:37,223
-[sobbing continues]
-[Min-gyu clears throat]

896
00:50:41,310 --> 00:50:42,895
[Min-gyu clears throat]

897
00:50:48,943 --> 00:50:52,071
-[keypad beeping]
-[door opens]

898
00:50:54,115 --> 00:50:56,200
[footsteps approaching]

899
00:50:58,786 --> 00:50:59,704
Hey there.

900
00:51:00,329 --> 00:51:01,706
Come and have some tea.

901
00:51:01,789 --> 00:51:03,374
So did you have a good day today?

902
00:51:03,958 --> 00:51:04,834
Yep.

903
00:51:04,917 --> 00:51:08,212
Like you said, I did absolutely nothing
and spent the day being useless.

904
00:51:08,296 --> 00:51:09,881
Hmm… Very well done.

905
00:51:12,383 --> 00:51:13,384
Ta-da.

906
00:51:17,138 --> 00:51:18,139
What are they for?

907
00:51:18,222 --> 00:51:20,558
It's your graduation gift from SAEUM.

908
00:51:20,641 --> 00:51:22,518
Thank you for all your hard work.

909
00:51:22,602 --> 00:51:25,229
Mr. Kang, you were
the best boss I ever had.

910
00:51:30,610 --> 00:51:31,611
Thank you.

911
00:51:32,486 --> 00:51:35,281
In that case, shall we graduate
from you calling me "Mr. Kang"?

912
00:51:36,240 --> 00:51:37,074
What?

913
00:51:37,158 --> 00:51:38,951
Well, I'm not your boss anymore.

914
00:51:39,785 --> 00:51:40,786
Right.

915
00:51:41,329 --> 00:51:42,330
Then…

916
00:51:43,456 --> 00:51:44,457
Si-woo.

917
00:51:45,750 --> 00:51:46,876
Mmm, Ji-yoon.

918
00:51:49,378 --> 00:51:51,088
Put your mug down for a second.

919
00:51:51,172 --> 00:51:52,089
Why?

920
00:51:52,173 --> 00:51:53,966
You're going to spill it otherwise.

921
00:51:54,717 --> 00:51:57,511
[love ballad playing]

922
00:52:25,665 --> 00:52:27,667
[classical-jazz music playing]

923
00:52:31,003 --> 00:52:32,380
[Yeong-mook] Do you remember

924
00:52:33,297 --> 00:52:36,884
we ate out here on our very first date.

925
00:52:37,468 --> 00:52:38,594
I do.

926
00:52:39,512 --> 00:52:43,057
I brought a fancy bottle of wine,
and you just ordered sausages.

927
00:52:43,933 --> 00:52:47,269
Come on, who could've guessed
you'd bring wine back in those days?

928
00:52:47,770 --> 00:52:50,439
A drink back then always meant soju.

929
00:52:52,692 --> 00:52:56,320
You dragged out fixing that radio
for days just to flirt with me,

930
00:52:56,404 --> 00:52:59,281
using an apology
as an excuse to ask me out.

931
00:52:59,365 --> 00:53:01,951
I was expecting a romantic evening.

932
00:53:02,034 --> 00:53:03,035
Still,

933
00:53:03,744 --> 00:53:06,872
wine and sausage went
surprisingly well together, didn't they?

934
00:53:06,956 --> 00:53:08,124
[sighs]

935
00:53:09,375 --> 00:53:12,670
And I thought Ji-yoon and that guy
would be a good match too.

936
00:53:13,754 --> 00:53:16,382
Let the kids figure out their own lives.

937
00:53:16,966 --> 00:53:18,092
As for us…

938
00:53:19,176 --> 00:53:20,970
it's time we focused on our future.

939
00:53:22,638 --> 00:53:24,432
We can just graduate from marriage.

940
00:53:31,272 --> 00:53:33,482
If that's what you really want,

941
00:53:34,316 --> 00:53:35,317
then let's do it.

942
00:53:42,241 --> 00:53:43,576
Then marry me again.

943
00:53:47,455 --> 00:53:49,707
When your time comes to leave this world…

944
00:53:51,584 --> 00:53:53,085
I don't want you to be all alone.

945
00:53:56,839 --> 00:53:59,008
I'll try to make up for everything

946
00:53:59,759 --> 00:54:01,594
I didn't do for you in the past.

947
00:54:05,514 --> 00:54:07,433
Let me be with you… [sighs]

948
00:54:08,893 --> 00:54:10,478
…when you take your last breath.

949
00:54:14,356 --> 00:54:15,441
Are you

950
00:54:16,400 --> 00:54:19,028
using my deathbed as a pick-up line?

951
00:54:20,488 --> 00:54:22,114
Pick-up line? [chuckles]

952
00:54:23,199 --> 00:54:24,325
[sniffles]

953
00:54:31,499 --> 00:54:32,500
Hye-gyeong.

954
00:54:35,252 --> 00:54:36,587
Nothing else matters.

955
00:54:39,215 --> 00:54:40,382
I just want to

956
00:54:41,008 --> 00:54:42,384
outlive you by one day.

957
00:54:45,304 --> 00:54:49,058
-What are you doing, Yeong-mook?
-[laughing]

958
00:54:50,893 --> 00:54:51,977
I'm sorry.

959
00:54:53,270 --> 00:54:54,939
Forgive me, will you?

960
00:54:55,022 --> 00:54:56,899
[chuckles]

961
00:55:05,866 --> 00:55:08,953
Why did you come alone?
You said you were coming with your sister.

962
00:55:09,662 --> 00:55:12,414
Yeah, that was the plan,
but she went to see her boyfriend.

963
00:55:12,498 --> 00:55:13,707
Oh.

964
00:55:13,791 --> 00:55:16,210
If she has a boyfriend,
of course she should go see him.

965
00:55:16,293 --> 00:55:17,294
Of course.

966
00:55:18,045 --> 00:55:19,588
Boyfriend over family, I guess.

967
00:55:19,672 --> 00:55:21,090
[scoffs]

968
00:55:21,173 --> 00:55:23,050
Are you done with your interviews?

969
00:55:23,134 --> 00:55:25,553
I can let you use this space
whenever you need.

970
00:55:26,053 --> 00:55:29,765
Oh, I haven't decided on my next project.

971
00:55:30,349 --> 00:55:31,934
What kind of story do you want to tell?

972
00:55:32,017 --> 00:55:33,060
Well, this time…

973
00:55:33,769 --> 00:55:36,063
I wanna move away from pure office love

974
00:55:36,147 --> 00:55:38,274
and instead write a story

975
00:55:38,357 --> 00:55:41,318
about people who give their all
to both work and love.

976
00:55:42,236 --> 00:55:44,697
Drama is exploding at the workplace,

977
00:55:45,239 --> 00:55:47,283
and their love lives are a complete mess,

978
00:55:47,366 --> 00:55:50,035
so they suffer
and throw fits all the time,

979
00:55:50,536 --> 00:55:53,330
but they still… clock in tomorrow.

980
00:55:53,414 --> 00:55:54,540
Wow.

981
00:55:55,040 --> 00:55:56,292
So it's horror?

982
00:55:56,792 --> 00:55:58,210
Would an office worker read that?

983
00:55:58,294 --> 00:56:00,004
That's what I'm torn about.

984
00:56:01,755 --> 00:56:05,384
Should I stick to what sells
instead of what I actually wanna write?

985
00:56:08,179 --> 00:56:09,680
"404 FOUND."

986
00:56:10,264 --> 00:56:12,641
You know how when you browse the Internet

987
00:56:13,142 --> 00:56:15,895
it sometimes says "404 NOT FOUND"?

988
00:56:16,520 --> 00:56:19,148
Well, that means the server is running,

989
00:56:19,231 --> 00:56:21,358
but the corresponding page doesn't exist.

990
00:56:21,442 --> 00:56:22,985
"I do exist somewhere,

991
00:56:23,527 --> 00:56:25,112
but I can't find the answer."

992
00:56:25,696 --> 00:56:26,614
The thing is,

993
00:56:26,697 --> 00:56:29,950
404 isn't exactly a fatal system error.

994
00:56:30,034 --> 00:56:32,328
If you take a little break and reboot,

995
00:56:33,412 --> 00:56:34,955
you might just find it again.

996
00:56:35,456 --> 00:56:38,667
So you're saying if I get writer's block,

997
00:56:38,751 --> 00:56:40,836
I should just come here,
grab a drink, and unwind?

998
00:56:40,920 --> 00:56:42,254
Bingo.

999
00:56:42,338 --> 00:56:45,841
[laughing] Man, I totally fell for that.
[clicks tongue]

1000
00:56:45,925 --> 00:56:47,676
-Pour me another one.
-With pleasure.

1001
00:56:54,183 --> 00:56:57,686
[Yeong-mook] You always come here to clear
your head when you can't find the answer.

1002
00:57:00,731 --> 00:57:01,732
I'm going to spend

1003
00:57:02,566 --> 00:57:05,152
my time traveling with my wife
from now on,

1004
00:57:05,694 --> 00:57:07,863
so come fix things
and look after the place for me.

1005
00:57:10,658 --> 00:57:14,411
Take your time and figure out
what you want to do while you're at it.

1006
00:57:21,126 --> 00:57:24,171
Stop worrying about me
and just take care of yourself, Da-ra.

1007
00:57:24,880 --> 00:57:27,091
Don't just live on burgers, hmm?

1008
00:57:27,841 --> 00:57:29,718
And don't get hurt playing futsal.

1009
00:57:30,844 --> 00:57:33,305
All right.
I'll call you as soon as I land.

1010
00:57:37,685 --> 00:57:38,727
[sighs]

1011
00:57:39,561 --> 00:57:42,273
CALLING
MON AMOUR JAE-IN

1012
00:57:43,023 --> 00:57:44,400
[line ringing]

1013
00:57:47,152 --> 00:57:50,531
[operator] Your call cannot be connected.
You'll be redirected to--

1014
00:57:50,614 --> 00:57:51,615
[call ends]

1015
00:57:52,700 --> 00:57:54,702
I wonder why he won't pick up.

1016
00:58:03,252 --> 00:58:04,586
[line ringing]

1017
00:58:09,049 --> 00:58:10,301
[sighs]

1018
00:58:12,177 --> 00:58:13,220
Hello, Jae-in.

1019
00:58:14,346 --> 00:58:15,347
[Jae-in] No-ah.

1020
00:58:17,308 --> 00:58:19,310
[upbeat synth-pop playing]

1021
00:58:31,989 --> 00:58:33,615
What are you doing here?

1022
00:58:34,908 --> 00:58:36,452
I couldn't bear to send you off alone.

1023
00:58:42,207 --> 00:58:43,542
I'll drop you off.

1024
00:58:43,625 --> 00:58:45,294
Aw, Jae-in.

1025
00:58:52,593 --> 00:58:55,095
I never thought my first trip with you
would be to Senegal.

1026
00:58:55,179 --> 00:58:57,681
Wow. I love this a lot.

1027
00:58:57,765 --> 00:58:59,933
[laughing]

1028
00:59:03,729 --> 00:59:04,730
Thanks so much.

1029
00:59:04,813 --> 00:59:05,814
Don't mention it.

1030
00:59:18,494 --> 00:59:20,037
Working late again tonight?

1031
00:59:22,164 --> 00:59:24,166
Not at all. I'm just having fun here.

1032
00:59:24,249 --> 00:59:27,169
Anyone would think
you're building model kits or something.

1033
00:59:27,252 --> 00:59:28,253
Have you had dinner?

1034
00:59:29,046 --> 00:59:30,047
I'm unemployed, so…

1035
00:59:30,130 --> 00:59:32,758
-[scoffs] What about lunch?
-I had ramyeon.

1036
00:59:32,841 --> 00:59:35,344
Your lifestyle has seriously tanked
ever since you quit.

1037
00:59:35,928 --> 00:59:39,431
I thought you said health was
the one thing you'd never compromise on.

1038
00:59:41,141 --> 00:59:43,977
I'll be fine.
I have a naggy person by my side.

1039
00:59:44,061 --> 00:59:45,062
[gasps]

1040
00:59:53,070 --> 00:59:55,322
[gasps] Delicious.

1041
00:59:55,406 --> 00:59:56,657
How's your work coming along?

1042
00:59:56,740 --> 00:59:58,033
I've got a rough outline down.

1043
00:59:58,117 --> 00:59:59,618
Oh…

1044
01:00:00,202 --> 01:00:01,412
How are things for you?

1045
01:00:01,495 --> 01:00:04,206
The rookie is killing me
with a new mess-up every day.

1046
01:00:04,289 --> 01:00:06,583
-I don't wanna go to work tomorrow.
-[chuckles]

1047
01:00:07,167 --> 01:00:10,129
Then call in sick
and stay here with me instead.

1048
01:00:10,879 --> 01:00:12,047
Should I?

1049
01:00:12,965 --> 01:00:14,258
Do you mind if I join you?

1050
01:00:14,341 --> 01:00:15,843
[Si-woo] Unwind this first.

1051
01:00:15,926 --> 01:00:18,137
[gentle music playing]

1052
01:00:23,725 --> 01:00:24,852
And then after…

1053
01:00:27,104 --> 01:00:29,898
You detach this part, which reveals…

1054
01:00:29,982 --> 01:00:31,233
[Ji-yoon] Impressive.

1055
01:00:31,942 --> 01:00:34,445
Even the way you take things apart
is on another level.

1056
01:00:34,528 --> 01:00:37,114
-Try this one too.
-[Ji-yoon chuckles]

1057
01:01:11,732 --> 01:01:12,649
Take a seat.

1058
01:01:12,733 --> 01:01:14,318
What were you working on?

1059
01:01:14,860 --> 01:01:16,737
I was brainstorming some ideas, and…

1060
01:01:16,820 --> 01:01:18,822
[gentle music continues]

1061
01:01:21,241 --> 01:01:23,494
[laughs]

1062
01:01:23,577 --> 01:01:26,121
Please look for an office space
around Songwol-dong.

1063
01:01:26,205 --> 01:01:28,707
-It doesn't have to be that big.
-[cicadas buzzing]

1064
01:01:30,083 --> 01:01:33,253
-[Ji-yoon] Wow!
-Sleep. I'll carry you like this.

1065
01:01:34,046 --> 01:01:35,214
[Ji-yoon chuckles]

1066
01:01:35,297 --> 01:01:36,632
[Si-woo] But you know what?

1067
01:01:36,715 --> 01:01:37,925
[Ji-yoon] What?

1068
01:01:43,514 --> 01:01:46,934
6 MONTHS LATER

1069
01:01:56,568 --> 01:01:59,780
When it comes to automotive audio,
it's really a battle against noise.

1070
01:01:59,863 --> 01:02:04,201
You have to be able to control engine hum,
road noise, and even wind sound.

1071
01:02:04,284 --> 01:02:07,955
Well, a microphone needs to sense
the noise inside the car.

1072
01:02:08,038 --> 01:02:09,998
MARKET LANDSCAPE - LIMITATIONS
OF LEGACY AUTOMOTIVE

1073
01:02:10,082 --> 01:02:13,377
A speaker can put out
the exact opposite phase.

1074
01:02:13,460 --> 01:02:15,128
Besides canceling out noise,

1075
01:02:15,212 --> 01:02:18,257
the system should read the driver's
emotions and adjust accordingly.

1076
01:02:19,007 --> 01:02:20,175
What do you think, Toto?

1077
01:02:20,759 --> 01:02:23,929
If I tell you, you're just going to dump
all the work on me again.

1078
01:02:24,012 --> 01:02:26,974
That's only because you're the most
hardworking teammate we have.

1079
01:02:27,057 --> 01:02:28,559
Stop gaslighting me.

1080
01:02:28,642 --> 01:02:30,852
Keep this up, and I'm taking a PTO day.

1081
01:02:30,936 --> 01:02:32,145
[chuckling]

1082
01:02:33,480 --> 01:02:34,648
[person] Manager Cha!

1083
01:02:35,524 --> 01:02:38,527
[upbeat music playing]

1084
01:02:42,823 --> 01:02:43,740
CHA JI-YOON

1085
01:02:43,824 --> 01:02:45,534
[Na-ri] Ms. Cha!

1086
01:03:01,466 --> 01:03:02,593
Have you all eaten already?

1087
01:03:02,676 --> 01:03:04,094
[all] Yes, Ms. Cha.

1088
01:03:04,177 --> 01:03:05,596
So, let's start the first meeting

1089
01:03:05,679 --> 01:03:09,016
of the revived
Future Household Appliances Task Force.

1090
01:03:12,311 --> 01:03:13,478
Sweetie!

1091
01:03:15,439 --> 01:03:17,816
-[soft pop playing]
-[chuckles]

1092
01:03:20,402 --> 01:03:21,945
What brings you all the way out here?

1093
01:03:22,029 --> 01:03:23,947
I came so we can brave the commute.

1094
01:03:26,366 --> 01:03:28,243
Let's walk a bit first.

1095
01:03:28,327 --> 01:03:30,245
It'll be completely packed
if we get on now.

1096
01:03:31,163 --> 01:03:32,164
Okay.

1097
01:03:42,341 --> 01:03:45,344
[Ji-yoon] We can't do this,
we can't do that. [sighs]

1098
01:03:45,427 --> 01:03:48,889
I mean, if they shoot down everything,
what are we supposed to work on?

1099
01:03:48,972 --> 01:03:52,017
At this rate, I think
we're going to lose everything, huh,

1100
01:03:52,100 --> 01:03:54,061
to our competi-- [gasps, exclaims]

1101
01:04:10,369 --> 01:04:12,454
A fall at your age can mean broken bones.

1102
01:04:14,164 --> 01:04:15,374
[chuckles]

1103
01:04:17,793 --> 01:04:19,961
[lighthearted music playing]

1104
01:04:23,048 --> 01:04:24,383
Let's get married then,

1105
01:04:24,466 --> 01:04:26,301
before we get any older, Ji-yoon.

1106
01:04:29,262 --> 01:04:30,389
Wow.

1107
01:04:31,306 --> 01:04:33,016
It's an actual ring this time.

1108
01:04:33,600 --> 01:04:35,102
So I'm taking it that means yes?

1109
01:04:37,979 --> 01:04:40,232
Hmm… Sorry.

1110
01:04:41,525 --> 01:04:42,401
Again?

1111
01:04:43,193 --> 01:04:44,569
This time…

1112
01:04:52,536 --> 01:04:53,995
I should be the one to propose.

1113
01:04:58,041 --> 01:05:01,128
But, you see,
I'm a little busy these days.

1114
01:05:01,795 --> 01:05:03,922
Can I put it on you after this project?

1115
01:05:04,005 --> 01:05:06,133
By that point,
we'll be getting matching hearing aids.

1116
01:05:06,216 --> 01:05:08,343
[laughs]

1117
01:05:15,600 --> 01:05:18,103
I don't know
when we'll be getting married, but…

1118
01:05:23,817 --> 01:05:26,570
It'll be with me on one spring day.

1119
01:05:41,042 --> 01:05:42,627
[Ji-yoon] I love being in love.

1120
01:05:43,920 --> 01:05:46,089
[Si-woo] Because it makes
everything possible.

1121
01:05:49,509 --> 01:05:51,678
Let's get fried chicken and beer
before we head home.

1122
01:05:51,762 --> 01:05:53,221
Again? Aren't you sick of it?

1123
01:05:53,305 --> 01:05:56,433
You know I could never get sick
of fried chicken and beer.

1124
01:05:57,517 --> 01:05:59,186
[Si-woo] Even when
there's no map to follow,

1125
01:05:59,269 --> 01:06:01,813
even when we lose our way for a while,

1126
01:06:01,897 --> 01:06:04,065
the one thing that helps us find our way…

1127
01:06:04,149 --> 01:06:06,693
[Ji-yoon] Will always be love.

1128
01:06:08,236 --> 01:06:11,031
Oh. I'm staying over
at your place tonight.

1129
01:06:11,823 --> 01:06:13,909
My new place is just so cold.

1130
01:06:14,409 --> 01:06:16,161
Don't you have to go to work tomorrow?

1131
01:06:16,787 --> 01:06:17,788
Mmm.

1132
01:06:18,288 --> 01:06:20,165
I can't slack off on love because of work.

1133
01:06:22,292 --> 01:06:23,710
[both chuckle]

1134
01:06:27,547 --> 01:06:28,673
I love you.

1135
01:06:28,757 --> 01:06:31,301
[laughs] Love you too.

1136
01:06:35,388 --> 01:06:37,599
[both] I love being in love.

1137
01:06:37,682 --> 01:06:40,685
[music continues]

1138
01:06:54,991 --> 01:07:00,288
GREAT JOB TODAY

1139
01:07:00,372 --> 01:07:07,337
WE'RE SIGNING OFF NOW

1140
01:07:07,420 --> 01:07:08,839
WE THANK BAE YU-RAM
AND PARK SEO-HAM

1141
01:07:08,922 --> 01:07:10,340
FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCES

1142
01:07:10,423 --> 01:07:12,342
[theme music playing]

